# junk.env.example — the addresses seed_junk.sh carries between phases.
#
#   cp junk.env.example junk.env      # junk.env IS gitignored (`*.env`)
#   ./seed_junk.sh check
#
# ⚠ THE FIGURES ARE NOT IN THIS FILE. Price, the map ceiling and the canary
#   divisor are SHIPPED DEFAULTS inside seed_junk.sh, because that is the file
#   that broadcasts and `pool_seeds.py` parses them straight out of it. Putting
#   a copy here would be the fourth copy of a number, which is the failure
#   pool_seeds.py's own header is about. Override them in the environment for a
#   one-off; change them in the script to change the posted rule.
#
# ⚠ PRIVATE_KEY IS NOT IN THIS FILE AND MUST NOT BE ADDED TO IT.

# The reserve. BLANK until ELO launches — CHECKLIST.md step 1 is the barrier,
# and `./seed_junk.sh check` prints "<unset>" rather than defaulting to the
# retired coin. A pool seeded against SCRY would be welded to it.
RESERVE_TOKEN=""

# Junk. Blank until `./seed_junk.sh deploy --arm` has run.
JUNK_TOKEN=""

# The wallet holding the opening-buy position — the seed is sized off ITS
# balance, so this must be the wallet that actually took the dev buy
# (ELO_BUY_RECIPIENT in elo.env, which defaults to ELO_DEPLOYER).
SEED_WALLET=""

# Written by `./seed_junk.sh record --pool` after the canary lands. `readback`
# refuses without it, which is deliberate: reading a pool you have not recorded
# is how you verify the wrong address.
JUNK_POOL=""

# Optional. Where the LP position NFT lands. Defaults to SEED_WALLET.
# POOLS.md §2.5: the operator's own wallet, never the meter/agency/facilitator.
LP_RECIPIENT=""

# ── MINT AUTHORITY — needed for `granary`, not for the pool ─────────────────
# The pool can be seeded and traded with the deploy wallet still holding the
# minter slot. These two are for the day Gates can actually pay a player.

# The wallet the GAME SERVER signs with. It becomes the granary's grantee and
# calls granary.mint(player, amount) on extraction. NOT the deploy wallet: a
# grant is per-caller, and the point of the granary is that the key doing the
# minting is capped rather than trusted.
GAME_MINTER=""

# Whole JUNK a season may mint AT MOST. Gates starts a new game the last
# Thursday of every month, and EloGranary caps per UTC DAY — so this is
# converted by script/season_cap.py, which has to exist because last-Thursday
# seasons alternate 28 and 35 days.
#
# ⚠ NO DEFAULT, AND `granary` REFUSES WITHOUT IT. DeployGranary.s.sol falls
#   back to 250e18, sane for the retired MYRRH farm and ~4 orders of magnitude
#   off for a play coin — and it would not fail, because the granary CLAMPS:
#   every extraction past the first few would quietly pay short.
SEASON_BUDGET_JUNK=""

# Written by `./seed_junk.sh record --granary`.
JUNK_GRANARY=""

# The LP position's tokenId, from the seed receipt (the NFT the NPM mints to
# LP_RECIPIENT). `fees` and `compound` both refuse without it — and that
# refusal is the point: a position nobody recorded is a position whose fees
# nobody collects, which is indistinguishable from a pool that earned nothing.
JUNK_POSITION=""
